        heading: "What can change the scope and cost",
        body: "Humidity changes everything — dry heat and humid heat are different engineering problems. Building use matters too: a data room and an office have nothing in common thermally. And existing buildings being retrofitted for hotter conditions face constraints new construction doesn't.\n\nDesign for the climate you have, not the climate the catalog assumes.",
